    "summary": "This intricate, hand-woven textile was likely produced on a back-strap or upright loom. The <em>binakol</em> block pattern creates a strong optical effect, organized in vertical registers separated by broad, dark stripes with narrow, red accents. The central design is a variant of the whirlpool motif known as <em>kusikos</em>, in which alternating light and dark squares appear to spiral or recede.",
